theory.intro:
Reading an exponential model means saying what its numbers mean in the real situation. The value of $k$ is the amount at the start, the base gives the percentage change each period, and the model only makes sense over a limited range.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.4,0) -- (5.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-0.4) -- (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:5.2,samples=100,variable=\x,->] plot ({\x},{3.6*exp(-\x*0.5)});
\fill (0,3.6) circle (2pt);
\node[right] at (0.3,4.0) {$(0,k)$ initial value};
\node[below] at (3.2,-0.15) {asymptote $y=0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The graph shows the value $A$ dollars of a savings account after $n$ years.
Write down the vertical intercept and state what it means in this context.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=7.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.4,xmax=5.6,ymin=-200,ymax=3400,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5},ytick={0,400,...,3200},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$n$},ylabel={$A$},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,->,domain=0:5,samples=100] {2000*exp(x*ln(1.1))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

